[font=Georgia]
[center]
[color=#D4AF37][h1]Embers of Empire[/h1]
[color=#E8DCC4][i]A Roman Restoration[/i][/color]
[/center]

Embers of Empire expands the vanilla Roman restoration experience with new paths for rebuilding the Western Roman Empire, restoring Roman institutions, and shaping a renewed Greco-Roman world.

[h2][color=#D4AF37]Current Compatibility[/color][/h2]

The latest version is ready for CK3 1.19. Start a new campaign to meet the newly added historical rulers and see their stories reflected in title history.

[color=#E8DCC4]
[h2][color=#D4AF37]Latest Update - Version 1.18.4[/color][/h2]

[i]Maintenance & History Update[/i]

The latest update brings EoE firmly into CK3 1.19 while giving the restored Roman world a deeper past.

[list]
[*][b]Five new title histories:[/b] follow the rulers of the Western Roman Empire, Bosporan Kingdom, Gallic Empire, Imperial Pontificate, and Carausian Britannia.
[*][b]Historical characters and dynasties:[/b] discover emperors, rival claimants, royal families, heraldry, and sourced epithets from across the Roman world.
[*][b]A stronger Western restoration:[/b] improved wars, provincial integration and decisions.
[*][b]More complete faiths and cultures:[/b] repaired religious content, clearer choices, missing names, and richer English text.
[*][b]Hundreds of fixes and refinements:[/b] updated events, traits, monuments, maps, icons, tooltips, and compatibility for CK3 1.19.
[/list]

[i]Start a new campaign to experience the new historical rulers and title histories.[/i]
[/color]
[hr]

[h2][color=#D4AF37]Content Update 2.1[/color][/h2]

[b]New Buildings And Decisions[/b]

[list]
[*]Temple of Jupiter Optimus Maximus
[*]Temple of Sol Invictus
[*]Circus of Nero
[*]Palatine Palace
[*]Great Projects: [b]Restore the Temple of Jupiter Optimus Maximus[/b] and [b]Restore the Palatine Hill[/b]
[*]Decision: Destroy the Church of Saint Peter
[/list]

[b]New Faith And Tenets[/b]

[list]
[*]New Faith: [b]Orphism[/b]
[*]New Tenets: [b]Sophrosynia, Bacchanalia, and Eleusinia[/b]
[/list]

[b]Fixes[/b]

[list]
[*]Fixed Germania not being properly integrated when forming the Western Roman Empire.
[*]Fixed Dacia not being properly integrated when forming the Western Roman Empire.
[/list]

[i]More special buildings and additional Great Projects are planned for future updates.[/i]

[b]CONTENT UPDATE 2.1 IS NOT SAVEGAME COMPATIBLE.[/b]
[hr]

[h2][color=#D4AF37]Restore Rome Your Way[/color][/h2]

Rebuilding Rome should feel like more than pressing a single decision. EoE turns restoration into a longer journey of conquest, faith, culture, and statecraft, with new choices for both the eastern and western Roman worlds.

[list]
[*] Expanded Western Roman restoration mechanics and reconquest content
[*] New Roman, Hellenic, Germanic, Druidic, Kushite, Orphic, and related religious content
[*] New cultural traditions and regional Roman cultures
[*] Decisions to restore institutions, provinces, monuments, temples, and settlement patterns
[*] New formable secular and religious titles
[*] New men-at-arms, great projects, and special buildings
[*] Roman-themed events, traits, coat of arms content, and visual assets
[/list]

[h3][color=#C9A227]Rebuild The Eternal City[/color][/h3]

An emperor needs more than a grand title. Restore the monuments of Rome, revive ancient sanctuaries, and leave a capital worthy of the empire you are rebuilding.

[list]
[*] Temple of Sol Invictus
[*] Circus of Nero
[*] Palatine Palace
[*] Restoration projects for the Temple of Jupiter Optimus Maximus and the Palatine Hill
[*] Decision content involving the Church of Saint Peter
[/list]

[h3][color=#C9A227]Historical Title History - Work In Progress[/color][/h3]

Rome was built by generations of emperors, kings, rivals, and ambitious families. This ongoing project gives several of the mod's restored titles a real historical past, with researched rulers and dynasties waiting in their title history.

The first completed histories cover:

[list]
[*] Western Roman Empire
[*] Bosporan Kingdom
[*] Gallic Empire
[*] Imperial Pontificate
[*] Carausian Britannia
[/list]

This part of the mod is still a work in progress. More suitable titles, rulers, families, and historical details will be added over time.

[h2][color=#D4AF37]Planned Features[/color][/h2]

EoE is still growing. Current ideas and ongoing projects include:

[list]
[*] More special buildings and ambitious Great Projects
[*] Additional historical title histories, rulers, and dynasties
[*] New alternative paths of Roman conquest and restoration
[*] Continued polish for religions, cultures, decisions, and official compatibility patches
[/list]

These are plans rather than release promises, and their scope may change as development continues.

[h2][color=#D4AF37]Compatibility And Load Order[/color][/h2]

Place Embers of Empire before any EoE compatibility patches in your load order.

EoE touches many parts of the Roman world, so another large overhaul may try to reshape the same content. Use the dedicated patches below where available. If something unexpected happens, include your complete playset and load order when reporting it; that is often the fastest way to find the rival claimant.

[bgcolor=#1E2A1E][color=#D8E8C8]
[b]EoE is fully compatible with RICE.[/b] It has been tested repeatedly, and the two mods coexist without conflict.
[/color][/bgcolor]

